  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "In triangle \\(\\triangle ABC,\\) medians \\(AD\\) and \\(CE\\) intersect at \\(P,\\) \\(PE=1.5,\\) \\(PD=2,\\) and \\(DE=2.5.\\) What is the area of \\(AEDC?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\( 13 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\( 13.5 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\( 14 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\( 14.5 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\( 15 \\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "13.5"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2013-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(PE:PD:DE=1.5:2:2.5\\) \\(=3:4:5\\), triangle \\(DPE\\) is right at \\(P\\). Thus medians \\(AD\\) and \\(CE\\) are perpendicular.\n\nThe centroid divides each median in a \\(2:1\\) ratio, so \\(CE=3\\cdot PE=4.5\\) and \\(AD=3\\cdot PD=6\\).\n\nQuadrilateral \\(AEDC\\) has perpendicular diagonals \\(AD\\) and \\(CE\\), so its area is \\(\\frac12(AD)(CE)=\\frac12\\cdot6\\cdot4.5=13.5\\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Use the centroid ratio on both medians",
        "The \\(1.5,2,2.5\\) triangle is right"
      ],
